I walk back along the quiet street.
I walk straight ahead.
Soon I see the large square again.
Then I walk across the square.
Now I am standing by the museum.
I remember the woman's words: "Turn right."
At the museum I turn right.
I walk down a wide street.
I look ahead.
Finally I see something blue.
It is the water!
On the way I walk past a little café.
At last I walk all the way down to the water.
Now I am at the harbour.
The harbour is very large.
The wind is cold and fresh.
There are many boats on the water.
Here I stop.
I stand and look at the boats.
